"""Southern Barrens hub: a story speech, and names and places the old accept line used to carry."""

STORY = {
    'tau_road_south': ("I'm not asking you to fix it. I'm asking you to walk up and look at it, because I've asked four people and got four different mountains back. Go to where the Lift stood. The winch house is still bolted to the rock, and the cable runs out thirty feet and straight into granite. Past that, there's a line in the ground where the red dust stops and the leaf mould starts, as sharp as a knife cut. Stand on it, and tell me what's on the other side.", "Take a sprig of whatever grows on the far side, if you can. I'd like to hold it."),
    'tau_can_kodo_go_down': ("I sent somebody up to the Lift once already and got back the word that there were trees on it. I've had three years to make peace with that, and about four days to make peace with the rest. There's a way down now, and what I need to know is whether a kodo can take it, because a road a kodo can't walk is only a footpath with ambitions. Walk the whole thing, from where the timber stops at the head of the descent down to where the road forks on the valley floor. I'm asking about the slope, the footing and whether there's water in the first two days, and you'll only know that by putting your own feet on it.", 'Count the switchbacks as you go. A kodo turns wide, and every one of them matters.'),
    'sb_the_matriarchs_last_walk': ("There's a herd-mother out on the Field of Giants walking in circles. She's been at it a season, on the same ground, goring anything that comes near her, and the herders call her Old Mother Longhorn.\n\nShe isn't mad, and I need that said before I ask you. She lost a calf somewhere out there in the bones, and she's been looking for it ever since, and the circle is the search. The Aged Kodo of her herd walk it with her, and they won't let you near her while they're standing. I won't do it myself. I think it would be bad luck for a man in my trade, and you can think what you like of that.\n\nI pay well, though, and I'd ask you to be quick about it. She's been grieving long enough.", None),
    'sb_eyes_on_the_gate': ("I'm Zhuul, and I came down to the Waystation for a hot meal and a dry night, and I'm back up to the Keep at dawn.\n\nI've been lying in the grass outside Bael'dun Keep, north-west of here, for two months with a spyglass and a bad attitude, and one of those is professional. The dwarves have turned Bael'dun into a proper fortress, with riflemen on the walls and patrols working the yard on a rotation I could set a clock by. That isn't a mining camp protecting itself, mon. It's a garrison.\n\nI need the gate scouted and the Bael'dun Riflemen thinned before one of them spots me. Walk up to the gate, look, and come back. I'd go myself, but I'd leave a trail through that grass you could follow from the wall.", None),
    'sb_ironvein': ("Sergeant Ironvein runs the east wall of Bael'dun Keep, north-west of here, and I've come to think he is the east wall. He drills the riflemen, and he walks the mastiffs himself at least twice a week, when the other sergeants only do it on paper. And he hammers every plan flat before it leaves the yard. I've watched three officers walk out of that gate with an idea and come back without it.\n\nMost garrisons rot from the inside, because nobody's willing to say no to a bad plan. If Ironvein falls, the east gate falls.\n\nHe's up on the walls among the Bael'dun Sergeants, so listen for the hammer. Dwarves fight better in lines than loose, so break the line first and take them one at a time after.", None),
    'sb_thrumbone': ("There's something out there older than the bones. Think about that, because I've had three years with it. Those ribs have been on that plain since before anybody wrote anything down about this continent, and there's a thing walking among them that was there first.\n\nThe wraiths gather round it. It walks a slow circle through the ribs, and when it does, the ground hums. I've felt that hum through my boots from a mile off. I call it Thrumbone. I've never seen it. I've had every chance, and I've turned away from all of them.\n\nI want it gone. Kill the Bone-Dust Wraiths first. Then, if you feel the ground start to sing, that's him. I'd run, and that's exactly why you're the one being paid. The Field of Giants is south of here.", None),
    'sb_vexa': ("At the bottom of the crater, past the guards and past everything, there's a queen called Vexa. The Sinkhole isn't just occupied by her, it's hers, the way a house is somebody's, and the Broodspiral below is her nursery.\n\nI want the stair. That's been my whole aim since last spring, and I won't pretend it's changed. But I'd also like the nursery intact, because a thing like that going down takes the ring with it, and nothing grows back in a crater. I can't have either while she's alive, and there's no deal to be made with her.\n\nGo down and find the nest at the centre. She's big and angry, and she won't stop. Neither should you, and that's the actual tactic. The Sinkhole Crater is south-east of here.", None),
    'sb_down_the_stair': ("Now for the stair. It doesn't go down, and you need that in your head before you're standing on it. It goes round. It's a spiral, and I've measured it twice and got two different answers, which I find personally insulting, because measuring well is the one thing nobody's ever disputed about me.\n\nThe Hive Drones and Hive Skulkers patrol the outer ring. Thin them so I can get in there with chalk, because an unchalked spiral is how a person ends up walking the same ring for hours convinced he's descending.\n\nKeep to the right-hand wall, and it'll bring you to the middle whether you like it or not. The Broodspiral is south-east of here, under the Sinkhole Crater.", None),
    'sb_the_tenders': ("Past the outer ring, the tunnel widens into a brood chamber. The things that tend it are called brood tenders, and I've been told they're quite gentle.\n\nI want to be careful about where that came from, because it matters. I was told it by somebody who isn't coming back. So I'm passing it on with that attached, rather than letting it sit in your head as a fact, which is more than anyone did for me when I started this dig.\n\nThe Broodkeeper sits at the head of the chamber, behind a pair of resin pillars. You'll see them from the entry, because they're the only straight lines down there. Kill the Brood Tenders first, then the Broodkeeper. And stay out of the green. The green isn't for you. The Broodspiral is south-east of here.", None),
}
